    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0461" n="373" xml:id="pg373"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Smith.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 146.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copies of two letters as follows:
                    From the News and Courier, of Charleston, S. C., elated March 7, and from the
                    secretary of the Merchants’ Exchange of the same city, dated March 9. The former
                    covers a check for $885.34, the latter, $110, the proceeds of which are to be
                    applied to the relief of the Russian sufferers, as directed by my telegram of
                    even date herewith. I append a copy of the telegram on the overleaf.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>



